From 2db16e13be5842588bb11f472a9092ef4cddee58 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: abhay-byte <abhay02delhi@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 04:37:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] jm-v7 096: strided index min/max search, folded into small
 direct draws

Every v6/v7 indexed draw went WRITE_VALUE (init) -> index_minmax_search
-> indexed-indirect helper -> vertex/tiler, chained. The search gave
each thread 1024 consecutive indices: lanes read 1-4 KiB apart, and a
300-index draw was one thread doing 300 dependent loads, plus two global
atomics per thread (perf review item 3).

- The search is strided (lane t reads t, t + n, ...), about 64 indices
  per lane over at most 64 workgroups, with a workgroup reduction in
  local memory and one atomic pair per workgroup.
- With one workgroup (direct draws up to 4096 indices, or small index
  buffers) lane 0 stores the result itself and the WRITE_VALUE init job
  is dropped.
- A direct DrawIndexed of at most 4096 indices whose vertex shader does
  not write memory runs panlib_draw_indexed_indirect_minmax_helper: one
  64-lane workgroup searches, lane 0 stores the range (the geometry
  emulation reads it) and patches the draw as the old helper did. One
  job instead of three. Memory-writing vertex shaders keep the separate
  search, since the vs_ref clear/mark jobs need the range before the
  helper.

Vulkan has no way for the app to give the index bounds, so the search
cannot be skipped outright.

PANVK_V7_MINMAX=nofold keeps the separate search; =0 also keeps the
WRITE_VALUE init and atomics for every search (pre-096 job layout).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
